# The Docker build context, trimmed to what the images actually copy.
#
# There was no .dockerignore, so every `docker build` here shipped the whole checkout to the daemon
# -- including `.venv`, which `cluster-e2e` creates with `uv sync` *before* it builds the workload
# image, and which is several gigabytes of already-installed dependencies the image installs again
# from the lockfile. None of it reached an image (the COPYs are selective), it was just carried.
#
# Kept deliberately narrow: local caches and build outputs only. Nothing here is an input to any
# image, and `.git` is *not* excluded -- the version is static now, but excluding a directory on the
# theory that nothing reads it is how a build starts failing for a reason nobody can see.
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
rust/target/
dist/
